message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite it as below."
title: "AgentTrajectorySentinel: Real-Time Detection and Repair of LLM Agent Failures"
abstract: >-
  A two-layer system for catching LLM agent failures while they happen. A
  one-class behavioural monitor (echo-state-network CUSUM ensembles fit on
  healthy runs only) scores every step causally, and a deterministic
  verification layer recomputes a run's answer from the tool results that run
  actually received. Detection is closed into repair by rolling a flagged run
  back to its last fact-gathering step and re-running it, which lifts task
  success from 52% to 73% for about one extra model call per run. The
  repository ships 2,823 committed agent episodes across 25 corpora, four agent
  models, three frameworks, and the full evaluation harness. The MIT licence
  below covers the software; recorded model output carries the terms of the
  model that produced it, itemised in DATA_CARD.md and traces/NOTICE_gemini.md.
